{"seq":19,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-member-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T13:38:24.837Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a955365049d90bf62956a642df47183dc18fa7c95c9dfedd101aecc728179caa","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the team digests. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. A patch went in on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through fine. The same note has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other two North notes (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers. The Central notes have tickets too (#4409, #4412, FR-882), but those are Central accounts, not QFL.\n\nOne thing to check before #4419 goes in the weekly notes: Marcus's handoff note from 14 Jul 2025 (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes) gives #4419 as \"Gate 3 printer lag\", a BOL printout delay. That doesn't match Moss's barcode-scanner description, and I can't tell from the notes which one is right."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
